---
import Terminal from "../components/Terminal.astro";
---

<div class="section-title">🦆 yazi</div>
<p class="desc-block">
  <a href="https://yazi-rs.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">yazi</a> — blazing fast terminal file manager
  written in Rust. Three columns (parent · current · preview) with syntax-highlighted previews via bat, and image
  previews in Ghostty.
</p>

<h3>In the terminal</h3>
<Terminal id="yazi" />

<h3>Shell wrapper (<code>.zshrc</code>)</h3>
<p class="desc-block"><code>y</code> opens yazi and <code>cd</code>s into the directory you were in when you quit.</p>
<div class="codeblock">{`function y() {
    local tmp="$(mktemp -t "yazi-cwd.XXXXXX")"
    yazi --cwd-file="$tmp" "$@"
    local cwd="$(cat -- "$tmp")"
    if [ -n "$cwd" ] && [ "$cwd" != "$PWD" ]; then
        cd -- "$cwd"
    fi
    rm -f -- "$tmp"
}`}</div>
